 # Working notes: 6bbf6747b137
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Current rule and generated subset
+
+Count color-1 cells in row 0. In the remaining rows, retain each same-color,
+4-connected component with exactly that many cells, preserving its color and
+position; erase the header and all other components. The canonical Racket rule
+is unchanged. Its program SHA-256 is
+`6198b0a067b4fffba296a03351abbfb7dee19d04a78420c132750c5f826d1cb4`.
+
+Version 1.2.0 ordinarily samples exactly three isolated body blobs with distinct
+sizes and colors. One size equals K; the two distractor sizes are the smallest
+members of 2..6 other than K. This is a subset of the reference task: the canonical
+test input has four body objects. `self_check` accepts that canonical case and
+checks the input domain, not the entire three-object generation grammar or a
+unique-selection certificate. Explicit `no_markers`, `no_matching_blob`, and
+`all_same_size` textures remain their fixed 9x9 edge fixtures.
+
+## Numeric controls and completion
+
+- K defaults to 2..6, including the canonical K=5 case; explicit K=1..6 works.
+  K=1 is an override-only boundary case.
+- Explicit `grid_h` and `grid_w` each accept 7..14 independently of difficulty.
+  Default sizes retain the old difficulty bands: easy 8x(8..9), hard
+  (9..10)x(9..10), otherwise (8..10)x(8..10).
+- These three numeric controls reject booleans, floats, strings, and values
+  outside their domains. `None` retains the existing no-override convention.
+- A failed blob placement retries the entire body, keeping the requested K and
+  all three target sizes. Exhausting 16 body attempts raises `RuntimeError`;
+  partial scenes are never returned. Each blob attempt retains the shared
+  helper's 80-try bound. Generation is deterministic for fixed arguments.
+- Domain checks reject malformed/ragged grids, non-integer or out-of-palette
+  cells, non-marker header colors, excess markers, and empty bodies. Zero
+  markers and zero/multiple matching blobs remain lawful edge cases.
+
+## Verified scope
+
+Baseline source `721ab5cb6c695e84b2bac04911d803a2cb8bd06d55b600217faf081c91429a15`
+ignored K overrides and rejected advertised 7/14 grid boundaries. See
+`checks/6bbf6747b137/baseline-probe.json`. The regression red run recorded 37
+failures, and a separate coverage regression proved default K=5/6 were absent.
+These are expected pre-repair failures, not current failures.
+
+The current 49 focused tests pass directly and through the staged task-test
+runner, including all three canonical Racket labels, all six K values on 7x7
+inputs, transient/permanent placement-failure injection, numeric validation,
+and the canonical four-object input. Evidence:
+`checks/6bbf6747b137/regression-green.xml` and
+`checks/6bbf6747b137/task-tests-after-v1/result.json`.
+
+The bounded adversarial probe in `workspace/probe_header_count.py` exercised
+96 boundary samples (K=1..6; four 7/14 dimension corners; four seeds), all with
+matching Racket labels and deterministic repeats. It also rejected 15 invalid
+numeric overrides and 11 malformed grids and verified that an injected permanent
+placement failure raises after 16 attempts. Its 3.686-second result and exact
+source/runtime hashes are in `checks/6bbf6747b137/adversarial.json`.
+
+## Remaining limitations
+
+Inherited palette metadata is still inaccurate: `palette_kind`, `palette_size`,
+`n_distinct_colors`, and helpful texture names do not control ordinary sampling.
+The sampler always picks three distinct body colors from 2..9 (four nonzero
+colors including the marker). `position_bias` and `density` remain fixed labels.
+The three explicit degenerate fixtures continue to bypass numeric overrides.
+These existing limitations were not silently redefined during the numeric
+repair. The next useful change is to remove or implement the inactive palette
+metadata and separately consider four-object coverage. No whole-repository
+battery or universal seed claim was made; a bounded retry can still fail visibly.
