 # Working notes: 6e8324f40386
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Current rule and structural contract
+
+The unchanged canonical Racket rule recolors each nonzero connected component:
+border-touching components become 2; strictly interior components become 8.
+Shapes, positions and the zero background are preserved.
+
+Version 2.2.0 makes structural overrides exact and independent of difficulty.
+`grid_h` accepts 6..14, `grid_w` 8..16, and `n` 2..5. The default difficulty
+bands remain 9..11 rows, 11..13 columns, and 3..4 components. An explicit
+`n_touching_border` accepts 1..n-1 and stays fixed across layout retries.
+Structural overrides require actual integers; `None` retains the default draw.
+Normal samples have distinct component colors and both recolor branches.
+`self_check` accepts the same component-count range, including all four canonical
+inputs, and checks exact counts when supplied in `meta`.
+
+The previous implementation rejected advertised structural overrides against
+narrow default bands, ignored `n_touching_border`, and rejected a two-component
+canonical input in `self_check`. The exact one-cell interior margin was also
+incorrectly excluded. Focused regressions reproduce these failures on the frozen
+source and pass on the repair.
+
+## Checked scope and remaining limits
+
+`checks/6e8324f40386/before-summary.json` binds the frozen source and 24 reproduced
+failures; the repaired focused suite has 31 passing tests. The short adversarial
+probe in `workspace/probe_structural.py` covers dimension/count extremes and
+integer/count-verifier rejection. Its Racket report at
+`checks/6e8324f40386/edge-racket/report.json` confirms all four canonical labels
+and 26 generated boundary-case labels against the unchanged rule.
+
+Individual axis ranges are not a guarantee that every joint layout fits. The
+6x8, n=5, n_touching_border=1 combination exhausted the 80-layout bound for seeds
+3 and 11: the bounded sampler did not find a layout for four interior motifs of
+3..5 cells under its conservative bounding-box padding. This is not an
+impossibility proof. Those two findings are retained in that report; requested
+counts are never relaxed. A next sampler improvement could add smaller motifs
+or less conservative cellwise separation, with separate distribution checks.
+
+Default sampling still uses larger grids and 3..5-cell motifs, so explicit
+canonical dimensions do not imply a full canonical-size/motif distribution.
+Legacy palette-related axes and helpful texture names remain ineffective; only
+the named degenerate textures select their fixed opt-in fixtures. This structural
+repair does not claim to fix those controls or establish lesson identifiability.
+No canonical rule, shared runtime, or issued test file changed.
