 The probe imports the selected generator by path and records its SHA-256 and declared rule hash. It reads the generator's actual `SEMANTIC_WITNESSES`, `SEMANTIC_RIVALS`, `WITNESS_RIVALS`, `CANONICAL_SHORTCUTS`, `LESSON_COMPETITORS`, `EXAMPLES_NEEDED`, and schedule rather than duplicating a rival-name list. It reports strict validity, unique inputs/outputs, exact-axis counts, changed-cell ranges, witness/rival disagreement, canonical shortcut fit, and all cyclic lesson starts.
 
 The report is finite generated-domain evidence. Do not interpret it as universal induction, masked-query accuracy, or correctness outside `self_check`.
+
+## Focused lesson-contract probe
+
+From the outer folder containing `review.py`, with the packet environment active:
+
+```bash
+python3 review.py run --receipt checks/9c75b1456763/lesson-command.json \
+  python3 generators/9c75b1456763/workspace/lesson_contract_probe.py \
+  --out ../checks/9c75b1456763/lesson-contract.json
+```
+
+Use new receipt/output paths. This bounded probe executes the unchanged canonical
+Racket rule on all four canonical inputs, checks masked and labeled query
+rotations, and attacks two boundaries: numeric/grid label validity and rival
+survival versus query disagreement. It binds the generator, probe and exact
+canonical program hashes and reports its elapsed time. Temporary test rivals
+are restored before return; they do not become production declarations.
